This is a great request. To adhere to SOLID principles (specifically Single Responsibility, Open/Closed, and Dependency Inversion), we need to decouple your architecture.
Here is the refactored solution.
Key Changes Made for SOLID:
 * SRP (Single Responsibility): The Repository no longer handles DTO mapping. A dedicated DifferenceMapper handles Entity-to-DTO conversion. The Repository only handles database interaction.
 * OCP (Open/Closed): We replaced the hardcoded JPQL IF NULL logic with JPA Specifications. This allows you to add new search filters (e.g., "Amount > X") without modifying the existing query logic—you just add a new Specification.
 * DIP (Dependency Inversion): The Controller now depends on an interface (IDifferenceService), not the concrete class.
 * Interface Segregation: The Service is defined by an interface, keeping the contract clear.
1. The DTOs (Data Transfer Objects)
Your DTOs remain mostly the same, but we ensure they are pure data carriers.
